      "message": "code change LGTM.  suggest adding more tests:\n\nTo ensure full test coverage for the changes in `parseAny(AnyObjectId)` and address the edge cases discussed, here are suggested test updates:\n\n1. **Verify `objects.add(r)` populates the object pool:**\n   - Update `assertParsedCommit` with `assertSame(actual, rw.lookupOrNull(expected));` to verify object pool registration on every parsed commit.\n   - Update `testParseCommit()` and `testParseAny()` to assert that calling `rw.parseCommit(c2)` / `rw.parseAny(c2)` a second time on the same `RevWalk` returns the exact same cached instance without additional disk I/O (`getCachedBytesCalls`).\n   - Fix code style: replace 2-space indentation with standard JGit tabs (`\\t`) and wrap lines at 80 columns.\n\n2. **Verify subclasses overriding 1-arg `createCommit(AnyObjectId)`:**\n   - Test that legacy subclasses overriding `createCommit(AnyObjectId)` (e.g. Gerrit\u0027s `CodeReviewRevWalk`) receive their custom `RevCommit` subclass from `parseAny`, cleanly fall back to disk (`getCachedBytesCalls \u003d\u003d 1`) without throwing `ClassCastException`, and populate the object pool.\n\n3. **Verify non-commits and unindexed commits when commit-graph is enabled:**\n   - Test `RevBlob`, `RevTree`, `RevTag`, and newly committed commits created after commit-graph generation through `parseAny` to verify they fall through cleanly to `parseNew(id, reader.open(id))` with expected caching and I/O counts.\n\n---\n\n### A. Imports to add / restore in `RevWalkCommitGraphTest.java`:\n```java\n// Under static imports (alphabetical between assertNull and assertTrue):\nimport static org.junit.Assert.assertSame;\n\n// Note: restore the empty line at line 25 between java.* and org.eclipse.jgit.* imports\n\n// Under org.eclipse.jgit.lib.* imports (alphabetical between Ref and filter):\nimport org.eclipse.jgit.lib.Repository;\n```\n\n### B. Updated `assertParsedCommit`:\n```java\n\tprivate void assertParsedCommit(RevCommit expected, RevCommit actual,\n\t\t\tint expectedGeneration, boolean expectBody) {\n\t\tassertTrue((actual.flags \u0026 RevWalk.PARSED) !\u003d 0);\n\t\tassertTrue(rw.shallowCommitsInitialized);\n\t\tassertEquals(expectedGeneration, actual.getGeneration());\n\t\tassertEquals(expected.getId(), actual.getId());\n\t\tassertEquals(expected.getTree(), actual.getTree());\n\t\tassertEquals(expected.getCommitTime(), actual.getCommitTime());\n\t\tassertArrayEquals(expected.getParents(), actual.getParents());\n\t\tassertSame(actual, rw.lookupOrNull(expected));\n\t\tif (expectBody) {\n\t\t\tassertNotNull(actual.getRawBuffer());\n\t\t\tassertArrayEquals(expected.getRawBuffer(),\n\t\t\t\t\tactual.getRawBuffer());\n\t\t\tassertEquals(expected.getFullMessage(),\n\t\t\t\t\tactual.getFullMessage());\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tassertNull(actual.getRawBuffer());\n\t\t}\n\t}\n```\n\n### C. Updated `testParseCommit()` (tabs, 80-col wrap, object pool checks):\n```java\n\t@Test\n\tpublic void testParseCommit() throws Exception {\n\t\tcommitFile(\"file1\", \"1\", \"master\");\n\t\tRevCommit c2 \u003d commitFile(\"file2\", \"2\", \"master\");\n\n\t\t// No commit-graph, retainBody \u003d true (default)\n\t\treinitializeRevWalk();\n\t\tassertTrue(rw.isRetainBody());\n\t\tRevCommit noGraphWithBody \u003d rw.parseCommit(c2);\n\t\tassertEquals(1, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\t\tassertParsedCommit(c2, noGraphWithBody,\n\t\t\t\tConstants.COMMIT_GENERATION_UNKNOWN, true);\n\t\tassertSame(noGraphWithBody, rw.lookupOrNull(c2));\n\t\tassertSame(noGraphWithBody, rw.parseCommit(c2));\n\t\tassertEquals(1, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\n\t\t// No commit-graph, retainBody \u003d false\n\t\treinitializeRevWalk();\n\t\trw.setRetainBody(false);\n\t\tassertFalse(rw.isRetainBody());\n\t\tRevCommit noGraphNoBody \u003d rw.parseCommit(c2);\n\t\tassertEquals(1, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\t\tassertParsedCommit(c2, noGraphNoBody,\n\t\t\t\tConstants.COMMIT_GENERATION_UNKNOWN, false);\n\t\tassertSame(noGraphNoBody, rw.lookupOrNull(c2));\n\t\tassertSame(noGraphNoBody, rw.parseCommit(c2));\n\t\tassertEquals(1, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\n\t\tenableAndWriteCommitGraph();\n\n\t\t// With commit-graph, retainBody \u003d true (default)\n\t\treinitializeRevWalk();\n\t\tassertTrue(rw.isRetainBody());\n\t\tRevCommit inGraphWithBody \u003d rw.parseCommit(c2);\n\t\tassertEquals(1, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\t\tassertParsedCommit(c2, inGraphWithBody, 2, true);\n\t\tassertSame(inGraphWithBody, rw.lookupOrNull(c2));\n\t\tassertSame(inGraphWithBody, rw.parseCommit(c2));\n\t\tassertEquals(1, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\n\t\t// With commit-graph, retainBody \u003d false\n\t\treinitializeRevWalk();\n\t\trw.setRetainBody(false);\n\t\tassertFalse(rw.isRetainBody());\n\t\tRevCommit inGraphNoBody \u003d rw.parseCommit(c2);\n\t\tassertEquals(0, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\t\tassertParsedCommit(c2, inGraphNoBody, 2, false);\n\t\tassertSame(inGraphNoBody, rw.lookupOrNull(c2));\n\t\tassertSame(inGraphNoBody, rw.parseCommit(c2));\n\t\tassertEquals(0, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\t}\n```\n\n### D. Updated `testParseAny()` (tabs, 80-col wrap, object pool checks):\n```java\n\t@Test\n\tpublic void testParseAny() throws Exception {\n\t\tcommitFile(\"file1\", \"1\", \"master\");\n\t\tRevCommit c2 \u003d commitFile(\"file2\", \"2\", \"master\");\n\n\t\t// No commit-graph, retainBody \u003d true (default)\n\t\treinitializeRevWalk();\n\t\tassertTrue(rw.isRetainBody());\n\t\tRevObject noGraphWithBody \u003d rw.parseAny(c2);\n\t\tassertTrue(noGraphWithBody instanceof RevCommit);\n\t\tassertEquals(1, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\t\tassertParsedCommit(c2, (RevCommit) noGraphWithBody,\n\t\t\t\tConstants.COMMIT_GENERATION_UNKNOWN, true);\n\t\tassertSame(noGraphWithBody, rw.lookupOrNull(c2));\n\t\tassertSame(noGraphWithBody, rw.parseAny(c2));\n\t\tassertEquals(1, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\n\t\t// No commit-graph, retainBody \u003d false\n\t\treinitializeRevWalk();\n\t\trw.setRetainBody(false);\n\t\tassertFalse(rw.isRetainBody());\n\t\tRevObject noGraphNoBody \u003d rw.parseAny(c2);\n\t\tassertTrue(noGraphNoBody instanceof RevCommit);\n\t\tassertEquals(1, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\t\tassertParsedCommit(c2, (RevCommit) noGraphNoBody,\n\t\t\t\tConstants.COMMIT_GENERATION_UNKNOWN, false);\n\t\tassertSame(noGraphNoBody, rw.lookupOrNull(c2));\n\t\tassertSame(noGraphNoBody, rw.parseAny(c2));\n\t\tassertEquals(1, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\n\t\tenableAndWriteCommitGraph();\n\n\t\t// With commit-graph, retainBody \u003d true (default)\n\t\treinitializeRevWalk();\n\t\tassertTrue(rw.isRetainBody());\n\t\tRevObject inGraphWithBody \u003d rw.parseAny(c2);\n\t\tassertTrue(inGraphWithBody instanceof RevCommit);\n\t\tassertEquals(1, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\t\tassertParsedCommit(c2, (RevCommit) inGraphWithBody, 2, true);\n\t\tassertSame(inGraphWithBody, rw.lookupOrNull(c2));\n\t\tassertSame(inGraphWithBody, rw.parseAny(c2));\n\t\tassertEquals(1, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\n\t\t// With commit-graph, retainBody \u003d false\n\t\treinitializeRevWalk();\n\t\trw.setRetainBody(false);\n\t\tassertFalse(rw.isRetainBody());\n\t\tRevObject inGraphNoBody \u003d rw.parseAny(c2);\n\t\tassertTrue(inGraphNoBody instanceof RevCommit);\n\t\tassertEquals(0, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\t\tassertParsedCommit(c2, (RevCommit) inGraphNoBody, 2, false);\n\t\tassertSame(inGraphNoBody, rw.lookupOrNull(c2));\n\t\tassertSame(inGraphNoBody, rw.parseAny(c2));\n\t\tassertEquals(0, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\t}\n```\n\n### E. New Test: Subclasses overriding 1-arg `createCommit(AnyObjectId)`:\n```java\n\t@Test\n\tpublic void testParseAnyWithSubclassOverridingCreateCommit()\n\t\t\tthrows Exception {\n\t\tcommitFile(\"file1\", \"1\", \"master\");\n\t\tRevCommit c2 \u003d commitFile(\"file2\", \"2\", \"master\");\n\n\t\tenableAndWriteCommitGraph();\n\n\t\t// Subclass overriding 1-arg createCommit(AnyObjectId)\n\t\ttry (CustomRevWalk customRw \u003d new CustomRevWalk(db)) {\n\t\t\tcustomRw.setRetainBody(false);\n\t\t\tRevObject obj \u003d customRw.parseAny(c2);\n\t\t\tassertTrue(obj instanceof CustomRevCommit);\n\t\t\tassertTrue((obj.flags \u0026 RevWalk.PARSED) !\u003d 0);\n\t\t\t// 1-arg createCommit sets graphPosition \u003d -1,\n\t\t\t// falling back to disk\n\t\t\tassertEquals(1, customRw.getCachedBytesCalls);\n\t\t\tassertSame(obj, customRw.lookupOrNull(c2));\n\t\t\tassertSame(obj, customRw.parseAny(c2));\n\t\t\tassertEquals(1, customRw.getCachedBytesCalls);\n\t\t}\n\n\t\t// Also verify retainBody \u003d true\n\t\ttry (CustomRevWalk customRw \u003d new CustomRevWalk(db)) {\n\t\t\tassertTrue(customRw.isRetainBody());\n\t\t\tRevObject obj \u003d customRw.parseAny(c2);\n\t\t\tassertTrue(obj instanceof CustomRevCommit);\n\t\t\tassertTrue((obj.flags \u0026 RevWalk.PARSED) !\u003d 0);\n\t\t\tassertEquals(1, customRw.getCachedBytesCalls);\n\t\t\tassertNotNull(((RevCommit) obj).getRawBuffer());\n\t\t\tassertSame(obj, customRw.lookupOrNull(c2));\n\t\t\tassertSame(obj, customRw.parseAny(c2));\n\t\t\tassertEquals(1, customRw.getCachedBytesCalls);\n\t\t}\n\t}\n```\n\n### F. New Test: Non-commits and commits not in commit-graph:\n```java\n\t@Test\n\tpublic void testParseAnyNonCommitAndCommitNotInGraph()\n\t\t\tthrows Exception {\n\t\tcommitFile(\"file1\", \"1\", \"master\");\n\t\tRevCommit c2 \u003d commitFile(\"file2\", \"2\", \"master\");\n\n\t\tenableAndWriteCommitGraph();\n\n\t\t// Commit created after commit-graph generation (not in\n\t\t// commit-graph)\n\t\tRevCommit c3 \u003d commitFile(\"file3\", \"3\", \"master\");\n\n\t\treinitializeRevWalk();\n\t\trw.setRetainBody(false);\n\t\tRevObject parsedC3 \u003d rw.parseAny(c3);\n\t\tassertTrue(parsedC3 instanceof RevCommit);\n\t\tassertEquals(1, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\t\tassertParsedCommit(c3, (RevCommit) parsedC3,\n\t\t\t\tConstants.COMMIT_GENERATION_UNKNOWN, false);\n\t\tassertSame(parsedC3, rw.lookupOrNull(c3));\n\t\tassertSame(parsedC3, rw.parseAny(c3));\n\t\tassertEquals(1, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\n\t\t// Non-commit: RevBlob\n\t\tRevBlob blob \u003d blob(\"test blob content\");\n\t\treinitializeRevWalk();\n\t\trw.setRetainBody(false);\n\t\tRevObject parsedBlob \u003d rw.parseAny(blob);\n\t\tassertTrue(parsedBlob instanceof RevBlob);\n\t\tassertEquals(blob.getId(), parsedBlob.getId());\n\t\tassertTrue((parsedBlob.flags \u0026 RevWalk.PARSED) !\u003d 0);\n\t\tassertEquals(0, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\t\tassertSame(parsedBlob, rw.lookupOrNull(blob));\n\t\tassertSame(parsedBlob, rw.parseAny(blob));\n\t\tassertEquals(0, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\n\t\t// Non-commit: RevTree\n\t\tRevTree tree \u003d c2.getTree();\n\t\treinitializeRevWalk();\n\t\trw.setRetainBody(false);\n\t\tRevObject parsedTree \u003d rw.parseAny(tree);\n\t\tassertTrue(parsedTree instanceof RevTree);\n\t\tassertEquals(tree.getId(), parsedTree.getId());\n\t\tassertTrue((parsedTree.flags \u0026 RevWalk.PARSED) !\u003d 0);\n\t\tassertEquals(0, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\t\tassertSame(parsedTree, rw.lookupOrNull(tree));\n\t\tassertSame(parsedTree, rw.parseAny(tree));\n\t\tassertEquals(0, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\n\t\t// Non-commit: RevTag\n\t\tRevTag tag \u003d tag(\"v1.0\", c2);\n\t\treinitializeRevWalk();\n\t\trw.setRetainBody(false);\n\t\tRevObject parsedTag \u003d rw.parseAny(tag);\n\t\tassertTrue(parsedTag instanceof RevTag);\n\t\tassertEquals(tag.getId(), parsedTag.getId());\n\t\tassertTrue((parsedTag.flags \u0026 RevWalk.PARSED) !\u003d 0);\n\t\tassertEquals(1, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\t\tassertSame(parsedTag, rw.lookupOrNull(tag));\n\t\tassertSame(parsedTag, rw.parseAny(tag));\n\t\tassertEquals(1, getCachedBytesCalls);\n\t}\n```\n\n### G. Helper classes (add at the bottom of `RevWalkCommitGraphTest.java`):\n```java\n\tprivate static class CustomRevCommit extends RevCommit {\n\t\tCustomRevCommit(AnyObjectId id) {\n\t\t\tsuper(id);\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tprivate static class CustomRevWalk extends RevWalk {\n\t\tint getCachedBytesCalls;\n\n\t\tCustomRevWalk(Repository repo) {\n\t\t\tsuper(repo);\n\t\t}\n\n\t\t@Override\n\t\tprotected RevCommit createCommit(AnyObjectId id) {\n\t\t\treturn new CustomRevCommit(id);\n\t\t}\n\n\t\t@Override\n\t\tbyte[] getCachedBytes(RevObject obj, ObjectLoader ldr)\n\t\t\t\tthrows LargeObjectException,\n\t\t\t\tMissingObjectException, IOException {\n\t\t\tgetCachedBytesCalls++;\n\t\t\treturn super.getCachedBytes(obj, ldr);\n\t\t}\n\t}\n```",
